{"thought":"Found that 'Death Touch' has power_id = 37. Now I need to find all superheroes with this power using Python to process the full CSV and join with superhero data.","action":"execute_python","action_input":{"code":"import csv\nimport sqlite3\n\n# Read hero_power.csv to find hero_ids with death touch (power_id=37)\nhero_ids_with_death_touch = set()\nwith open('csv/hero_power.csv', 'r') as f:\n    reader = csv.reader(f)\n    next(reader)  # skip header\n    for row in reader:\n        if len(row) >= 2 and row[1] == '37':\n            hero_ids_with_death_touch.add(int(row[0]))\n\nprint(f\"Hero IDs with Death Touch: {sorted(hero_ids_with_death_touch)}\")\n\n# Connect to database and get superhero names\nconn = sqlite3.connect('db/superhero.db')\ncursor = conn.cursor()\n\nif hero_ids_with_death_touch:\n    placeholders = ','.join(['?' for _ in hero_ids_with_death_touch])\n    cursor.execute(f'SELECT superhero_name FROM superhero WHERE id IN ({placeholders})', list(hero_ids_with_death_touch))\n    results = cursor.fetchall()\n    superhero_names = [row[0] for row in results if row[0]]\n    print(f\"Superheroes with Death Touch: {superhero_names}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"No heroes found with Death Touch\")\n\nconn.close()"}}
```
